  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) for constrained optimization, showing that QRAC encoding reduces qubit usage (≈7 qubits vs up to 20 for QAOA) on 100 multiple-knapsack instances while achieving similar solution quality (Magic rounding: 98% feasible, 70% optimal, 0.065 optimality gap). A hybrid QRAO + linear relaxation approach is tested on procurement optimization problems with ≥100 binary variables using a simulator.",
